<title>INDIA: India RBI sets up panel on non-bank finance firms.</title>
<headline>India RBI sets up panel on non-bank finance firms.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) on Wednesday said it set up a panel to suggest norms for regulation and supervision of non-bank finance companies.</p>
<p>The panel will be chaired by K.S.Shere, principal legal advisor of RBI.</p>
<p>Its terms of reference will include review of role of residuary non-banking finance companies including chit funds, an RBI statement said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
